        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 南方",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "南方 — nánfāng — \"the south of the country; southern China\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dōngtiān wǒmen zuò huǒchē qù nánfāng — In winter we take the train down south."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 方 (fāng) — four strokes: a dot, a long bar, a stroke that turns down and hooks, and a long stroke falling to the left. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "南方 (nánfāng) is built from 南 'south' and 方 (fāng) 'a quarter', both inherited from Middle Chinese, nom and pjang (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the second as the four quarters of the world."
            }
          ]
        },
